{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794987564,"nonce":"yGUuiOMnj+0H0lwv7SWLCR6c7Pc=","title":"[GitHub #79] Desktop accessibility: deliver the existing semantic tree to assistive technology (AccessKit or similar), add missing roles","message":"Source: https://github.com/project-blinc/Blinc/issues/79\nReporter: FreeSynergy\nGitHub state at capture: open\nReported: 2026-11-17T00:32:59Z; updated: 2026-11-17T00:32:59Z\nCaptured: 2026-11-18T07:38:25.958Z\n\nStatus: queued from the upstream report. This import does not claim local reproduction, implementation or a fix.\n\nTracking scope and expected outcome\n\nDeliver the existing semantic tree to desktop assistive technology, using AccessKit or an equivalent platform adapter. Preserve role, name, value, checked/selected/expanded/disabled state and focus notifications; add missing menu/menubar/separator/tree/treeitem/toolbar/dialog roles and distinct checkbox/radio menu-item semantics. Cover stable semantic identities and focus updates; use the reporter's offered Orca/Linux and NVDA/Windows validation when coordinating implementation.\n\nRelated local umbrella: 26f0d53 (Accessibility semantics and screen-reader support after keyboard navigation). This entry tracks GitHub #79 specifically; the umbrella retains the wider platform work.\n\nOriginal GitHub report\n\nHello, and thank you for Blinc.\n\nWe are building a shared menu model (menubar, menu, menuitem with checkbox and radio variants, separator, tree/treeitem, toolbar, dialog) on top of Blinc, and we want it to be usable with a screen reader.\n\n\nChecked against current upstream main:\n\n- `blinc_layout` already builds a platform-independent semantic tree: `RenderTree::accessibility_nodes()` (`crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/accessibility.rs:10`) returns nodes with role, label, value, disabled, selected, checked, expanded and focused (`crates/blinc_layout/src/accessibility.rs:60-76`). Labels come from `aria-label` / `aria-labelledby`, state from `aria-checked` / `aria-expanded` / `aria-selected` / `aria-disabled`.\n- The only consumer we found is the iOS backend (`crates/blinc_app/src/ios/accessibility.rs`, with the Swift side in `extensions/blinc_platform_ios/swift/BlincAccessibility.swift`). There is no consumer in `extensions/blinc_platform_desktop` and no dependency on AccessKit or a similar crate in any `Cargo.toml`. So on the desktop, nothing reaches assistive technology.\n- The role set is small: `AccessibilityRole` has Text, Heading, Button, Link, TextField, Checkbox, Switch, Radio, Slider, Tab, MenuItem, Image (`crates/blinc_layout/src/accessibility.rs:9-22`). `role=\"menuitem\"`, `\"menuitemcheckbox\"` and `\"menuitemradio\"` all map to `MenuItem` (`crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/accessibility.rs:206`). There is no role for menubar, menu, separator, tree, treeitem, toolbar or dialog (mapping at `renderer/accessibility.rs:190-235`).\n\nKeyboard operation works, so the menus can be driven, but nothing is announced on the desktop.\n\n\nOn desktop platforms, the existing semantic tree is delivered to the platform accessibility API, so a screen reader announces names, roles and states and follows focus.\n\n\nDesktop accessibility support, for example through AccessKit (https://github.com/AccessKit/accesskit), consuming the existing semantic tree, with:\n\n- the missing roles (menubar, menu, separator, tree, treeitem, toolbar, dialog) and a way to tell the checkbox/radio menu item variants apart,\n- the names and states that already exist (expanded, checked, selected, disabled) delivered to the platform,\n- focus notifications, so a screen reader follows the focused item.\n\n\nWe can test with Orca on Linux and NVDA on Windows, write test cases (a menu bar, a menu with checkbox/radio items, a tree, a dialog) against the semantic tree, and help with a pull request. If it helps, a small prototype or a short guide for wiring a widget to the accessibility tree would already be a good start. There is no hurry on our side.\n\nAlso tracked in git-bug in our fork FreeSynergy/Blinc (id ec4693d).","files":null}]}